# Selecting Research Collections for Digitization.

**Authors:** Hazen, Dan, Horrell, Jeffrey, Merrill-Oldham, Jan

## Abstract
Examines factors to consider when selecting materials to be digitized: copyrights; intellectual nature of the source materials; current and potential users; actual and anticipated nature of use; format and nature of the digital product; describing, delivering, and retaining the digital product; relationships to other digital efforts; and costs and benefits. Includes &quot;Selection for Digitizing: a decision-making matrix&quot;. (PEN)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ580150

